   "question": "La Yesca Dam Río Grande de Santiago completed 2012 inauguration",
   "answer": "La Yesca Dam is an embankment dam on the Santiago River (Río Grande de Santiago) in Mexico. It was inaugurated by President Felipe Calderón on 6 November 2012. Felipe de Jesús Calderón Hinojosa served as the 63rd president of Mexico from 2006 to 2012. Note: the claim describes him as a 'Spanish politician,' but the source identifies him as a Mexican politician.",
   "source": "La Yesca Dam - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Yesca_Dam ; Felipe Calderón - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felipe_Calder%C3%B3n",
   "excerpt": "La Yesca Dam is an embankment dam on the Santiago River 90 km (56 mi) northwest of Guadalajara on the border of Mexico's Nayarit and Jalisco states. ... The dam was inaugurated by President Felipe Calderón on 6 November 2012. ... Felipe de Jesús Calderón Hinojosa ... is a Mexican politician and lawyer who served as the 63rd president of Mexico from 2006 to 2012",
